AB  - This article defines enterprise architecture (EA) as a conceptual blueprint outlining an organization’s structure and operations, aimed at achieving present and future objectives. It emphasizes EA’s role in facilitating digital transformation by integrating legacy applications and processes into a unified environment, enabling improved alignment across business units. EA involves analysis, planning, design, and implementation tailored to shift entire organizations, not just IT. (By Alexander S. Gillis, published January 9, 2023.)
